From fe2709b5479acece00b06d1e9fb885af7af4066f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rogerbacardit <rogerbacardit@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:14:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] MIDI IN is machine-level: the same channels in every set

The channels describe the rig on USB-A (a KeyStep Pro's tracks), not the
song, and a new set started all SEL (user, 2026-11-16). They now live in
prefs.json beside the master volume, loaded on first use and saved on every
menu turn; a set's UI blob no longer carries or overrides them.

Gate: local suites (logic incl. midi-in.mjs prefs checks, app-loop,
screenshot, perf, source-rules, host-globals).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
